=== PARITY — web numeric pipeline ported VERBATIM (covenant #5) ===
  Source: GForcePanel.tsx reads useDriveDynamicsLatest(vehicleId, INTERVALS.REALTIME) and renders
  the 3-up StatCard grid when `hasAny`, else the EmptyState. Reproduced 1:1 in GForceProjector:
    lateral      = data.lateral_acceleration is number ? value : nil        (Double?)
    longitudinal = data.longitudinal_acceleration is number ? value : nil   (Double?)
    hasAny       = lateral != nil || longitudinal != nil
    magnitude    = (lateral != nil && longitudinal != nil)
                     ? (lat*lat + lon*lon).squareRoot() : nil      (web Math.sqrt; both-axes only)
    StatCard value = x != nil ? fmtNumber(x, 2) : '—'   ·   unit = "g"   ·   icon = gauge
  fmtNumber port (GForceFormat.number): locale-grouped, fixed 2 fraction digits, half-away-from-zero
  (NumberFormatter .halfUp == Intl halfExpand), safeNumber collapses NaN/±Inf → 0. The explicit `2`
  is the web literal (NOT getGlobalPrecision). G-force is dimensionless ("g") — no SI conversion,
  no Phase-48 unit-suffix concern. Worked example pinned by test (matches web regression suite
  DriveDynamicsPanels.test.tsx): {lateral 0.12, longitudinal -0.04} → "0.12" / "-0.04" /
  combined sqrt(0.016)=0.12649… → "0.13"; {} → empty state, labels gone.

